# Build context exclusions.
#
# Railway/Nixpacks copies the repository into the image before installing. Any
# of these that came along would be either wasted bytes or actively wrong — a
# host's `node_modules` holds platform-specific binaries that will not run in the
# container, and a stale `dist` would be overwritten by the build anyway.
#
# `.env` is listed for the obvious reason. It is already untracked, so it should
# never reach a build context from GitHub — this is the second lock on that door.

node_modules
**/node_modules

dist
**/dist
*.tsbuildinfo

.git
.github

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Hardhat build output. Regenerated by `npm run build --workspace @covenant/contracts`.
packages/contracts/artifacts
packages/contracts/cache
packages/contracts/typechain-types

npm-debug.log*
.DS_Store
